<details class="panel"><summary>Junk & spam filtering</summary><p>Incoming messages are checked with the server’s spam scanner. Suspicious mail goes to Junk; unavailable scans are held there for review. Strong server rejections and unavailable scans cannot be bypassed by an allowed-sender entry.</p><%= form_with url: dashboard_mail_account_path(account_id: @account.id), method: :patch, local: true do %><label>Filtering level<%= select_tag :spam_filter_level, options_for_select([["Standard", "standard"], ["Strict", "strict"]], @account.spam_filter_level) %></label><label>Allowed senders or domains<%= text_area_tag :allowed_senders, @account.allowed_senders.join("\n"), rows: 4, placeholder: "andrew@example.com\ntrusted-company.com" %></label><label>Blocked senders or domains<%= text_area_tag :blocked_senders, @account.blocked_senders.join("\n"), rows: 4 %></label><small>One address or domain per line, up to 200. Blocked senders take priority. Marking a message as spam moves it to Junk; these lists control future mail.</small><%= hidden_field_tag :auto_reply_enabled, @account.auto_reply_enabled? ? "1" : "0" %><%= hidden_field_tag :auto_template_id, @account.auto_template_id %><% if current_user.role == "super_admin" %><%= hidden_field_tag :enabled, @account.enabled? ? "1" : "0" %><%= hidden_field_tag :daily_limit, @account.daily_limit %><%= hidden_field_tag :storage_limit, @account.storage_limit %><% end %><%= submit_tag "Save spam settings" %><% end %></details>
